        <briefdescription>
<para>Returns the RPU core node IDs for the given device. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Returns the RPU core node IDs for the given device.</para><para><verbatim>    Looks up the RPU core by device ID. When TCM boot is requested, it
    resets and halts the core, releases its reset, and then sets the
    TCMBOOT field. Otherwise, it clears the TCMBOOT field directly.
</verbatim></para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>DeviceId</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Device ID of the RPU core to configure. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>TcmBootFlag</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Set to 1U to enable TCM boot; any other value disables TCM boot.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>None. If the core lookup or a reset operation fails, the function returns without modifying the TCMBOOT field. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
